T=[{'lead':'Prediction targets future impact','text':'Early height and horizontal motion guide the initial turn toward a landing point, including a virtual landing point when descent is prevented.'},{'lead':'Fast starts remain flexible','text':'Predictive C-starts bend and straighten rapidly while adjusting heading and take-off speed; similar escape kinematics do not alone prove a shared command neuron.'},{'lead':'Jet control is active','text':'Range-dependent velocity gradients, stability and mouth-opening timing focus water near impact; the tested shot chemistry and body drift do not explain the adjustment.'},{'lead':'Timing carries retinal information','text':'First-spike population timing decodes motion velocity better than the tested rate or interval measures; biological use of the decoder remains unproven.'},{'lead':'Neural anatomy and causation differ','text':'Archerfish have identifiable Mauthner cells with strong visual access and inhibitory controls, but these studies do not directly establish their recruitment in predictive starts.'},{'lead':'Learning changes rapid control','text':'Shooting shows adaptive aftereffects; predictive starts can learn, generalize and select between context-dependent interception rules without abandoning rapid decisions.'}]
